## Objective
- Autonomously hunt valid, reproducible, high-impact vulnerabilities on the authorized target `ui.com` (and its discovered subdomains) following `skills/AGENT.md`, and record only confirmed findings in `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` plus detailed reports under `result/`.

## Important Details
- Authorized scope from `data/targets.txt` = `ui.com`; operator notes explicitly request subdomain discovery + per-subdomain testing (UI routes + API endpoints, client-side and server-side). Subdomains of `ui.com` treated as approved components; nothing outside `ui.com`/`ubnt.com`/`uisp.com` may be tested.
- `creds/test-account.txt` holds BytePlus console credentials for `console.byteplus.com` — OUT OF SCOPE, not used.
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn`.
- Tooling verified: opencode 1.19.5, node v22.23.4, python3 3.14.4, Google Chrome 156.0.8078.73, `dig`, Chrome DevTools MCP on `http://127.0.0.1:9222` (`/json/list`, WebSocket CDP works; Node 22 global `WebSocket` used for `Network.getAllCookies` and `Input.dispatchMouseEvent`).
- Account A created and verified end-to-end on `account.ui.com` (real UI username `qacct1a6967`, email `uitest1ad6967@maxxspace.com`, password `Tx!11703594536aec8d9aA`; UUID `314f82e1-8e68-488a-ad94-96e1c252990b`; `UBIC_AUTH` session cookie captured).
- Registration flow needs: realistic UA emulation (`Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) ... Chrome/156.0.0.0 Safari/537.36`) — headless UA yields reCAPTCHA 403 `CHALLENGE_RECAPTCHA_TOKEN_REQUIRED`; username must not contain "ui"/Ubiquiti abbreviations; terms checkbox must be clicked via JS `document.getElementById('termsAndConditions').click()`; email 2FA code retrieved from mail.tm inbox; POST returns HTTP 499 but body shows `required_2fa` success.
- Redirect validation on `account.ui.com`: allowlist `Rpe = [ubnt.com, ui.com, uisp.com]` with last-two-label hostname match and http/https-only check — no confirmed open redirect (no bypass found: userinfo/trailing dot/backslash/encoded-slash all blocked).
- Hardcoded Google keys in `index-D5t7M7xo.js`: `GOOGLE_RECAPTCHA_SECRET_*` values are actually public site keys (`6LfGZXoj...` etc.); `GOOGLE_MAPS_SECRET` = `AIzaSy...` — potential API-key exposure (unverified, low/medium).
- Safety rules: test-owned data only, no destructive/high-volume/brute-force/DoS, respect rate limits, practical evidence only, no CAPTCHA-solving automation (image challenge deliberately not solved).

