## Objective
- Autonomously hunt valid, reproducible, high-impact vulnerabilities on the authorized target `ui.com` (and its discovered subdomains) following `skills/AGENT.md`, recording only confirmed findings in `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` with detailed reports under `result/`.

## Important Details
- Authorized scope from `data/targets.txt` = `ui.com`; operator notes request subdomain discovery + per-subdomain testing (UI routes + API endpoints, client-side and server-side). `ui.com` subdomains are approved; nothing outside `ui.com`/`ubnt.com`/`uisp.com` may be tested. `creds/test-account.txt` (BytePlus) is OUT OF SCOPE, unused.
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn`.
- Tooling: opencode 1.19.5, node v22.23.4, python3 3.14.4, Chrome 156.0.8078.73, `dig`, Chrome DevTools MCP on `http://127.0.0.1:9222` (Node 22 global WebSocket CDP helpers `/tmp/getcookies.mjs`, `/tmp/click.mjs`).
- Account A (verified): username `qacct1a6967`, email `uitest1ad6967@maxxspace.com`, password `Tx!11703594536aec8d9aA`, UUID `314f82e1-8e68-488a-ad94-96e1c252990b`; `UBIC_AUTH` cookie in `result/accounts/accountA-cookies.json`; mail.tm token in `result/creds/test-accounts.txt` (username already corrected to `qacct1a6967`).
- Registration quirks: requires realistic desktop Chrome UA; username cannot contain "ui"; terms checkbox clicked via JS; POST returns HTTP 499 on success (`required_2fa`); email 2FA code from mail.tm.
- Account B (UNRESOLVED): second inbox `uitestbtest2x@maxxspace.com` / `Tx!abc12345AA` (mail.tm id `6ae387d9c0e3a0d31d0067ff`) created; authenticated `POST /api/sso/v2/users` with `UBIC_AUTH` + empty captcha still `403 CHALLENGE_RECAPTCHA_TOKEN_REQUIRED`. Image reCAPTCHA will NOT be auto-solved.
- SSO write endpoints rate-limit aggressively: several rapid `PUT /user/self` → `429`.
- SSO JS method mapping: `hC`=GET, `_C`=POST, `vC`=PUT, `gC`=PATCH, `yC`=DELETE; profile update=`PUT /api/sso/v1/user/self`, settings=`PATCH /api/sso/v1/user/self/settings`; `PUT` accepts partial JSON.
- Redirect validation on `account.ui.com` uses allowlist `[ubnt.com, ui.com, uisp.com]` last-two-label match + http/https only; all bypass attempts blocked (userinfo/trailing dot/backslash/encoded slash).
- CORS: `sso.ui.com`, `billing.svc.ui.com`, `enterprise.svc.ui.com` reflect any `Origin` ending `.ui.com` with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`; `https://evil.example` is NOT reflected. `UBIC_AUTH` is `SameSite=Lax`, so exploitation needs a genuine `*.ui.com` origin (not standalone exploitable).
- Wildcard DNS: `*.ui.com` resolves to CloudFront (e.g. `108.156.91.x`), TLS cert `CN=*.ui.com`; unknown subdomains 302 to `https://account.ui.com/login?redirect=https://<host>/` (catch-all redirect loop for `evil.ui.com`, not a standalone vuln).
- CNAME findings: `dev-store.ui.com`/`dev.store.ui.com` → `ubnt-dev.myshopify.com` (Shopify password-protected, active); `help.ui.com` → `ubnt.zendesk.com`; `status.ui.com` → `r9sjd13s1zsp.stspg-customer.com`; `training.ui.com` → `saas.moonami.com`; `unifi.ui.com` → CloudFront. No dangling takeover.
- Google Maps key `AIzaSyBE3JpOF9gNSsb83dpZKLUqFkmBAsPr0-w` is referer-restricted (`REQUEST_DENIED: API keys with referer restrictions cannot be used with this API`) — NOT a finding. Stripe `pk_live_*` keys are public by design.
- Safety: test-owned data only, no destructive/high-volume/brute-force/DoS, respect rate limits, no CAPTCHA-solving automation.
- Source maps are unavailable (fetch returns SPA HTML / 406).

